# Chapter 6 checkpoint. Start the app first:
#   dotnet run --project AdventureWorks
# (https://localhost:7001 and http://localhost:5001, Development).
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see. A form POST
# needs the antiforgery cookie and token from a rendered page, so
# the saving, conflict and delete steps are in the browser and in
# the README's PowerShell section, not here.

@host = https://localhost:7001

###
# The product list page. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/Products

###
# The edit form for product 1. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/Products/Edit/1

###
# The route template needs an integer. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/Products/Edit/not-an-int

###
# An integer with no product: the handler returns NotFound.
# Expect 404
GET {{host}}/Products/Edit/999

###
# The Admin area page (not yet protected). Expect 200
GET {{host}}/Admin

###
# A POST without the antiforgery token is rejected before the
# handler runs. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/Products/Edit/1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

Input.Name=Trail+Helmet&Input.Price=29.99&Input.Version=1

###
# The pages and the APIs share one store.
# Expect 200 with "sku": "HLM-1001"
GET {{host}}/api/v2/products/1

###
# Earlier chapters' routes still answer. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog

###
# Expect 200 with "orderNumber": "AW-0001"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/ping
